WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.992
CSP is commonly delivered through the
Content-Security-Policy HTTP response header.

2
00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:12.515
When the browser receives the page,

3
00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:20.055
it reads the header and applies the policy
to resource loading and execution.

4
00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:26.332
There is also a
Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only header.

5
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:33.872
Report-only mode lets teams observe
violations without blocking behavior.

6
00:00:33.952 --> 00:00:41.985
That is extremely useful for rollout
because many applications have more frontend

7
00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:48.377
dependencies and inline behavior than
teams initially realize.

8
00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:52.359
A meta tag can provide some CSP behavior,

9
00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:58.980
but it has limitations and is not a
complete substitute for headers.

10
00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:06.864
Some directives and reporting behaviors
are not available or are less effective

11
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:09.239
through meta delivery.

12
00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:16.894
Headers are the normal production approach
because they are applied early and

13
00:01:16.974 --> 00:01:18.121
centrally.

14
00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:25.546
Teams should understand how their web
server, CDN, application framework,

15
00:01:25.626 --> 00:01:34.004
reverse proxy, and deployment platform set
headers so policies are consistent across

16
00:01:34.084 --> 00:01:34.772
pages.

17
00:01:34.852 --> 00:01:37.836
Rollout should be deliberate.

18
00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:43.539
Starting with report-only mode helps teams
collect data,

19
00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:51.653
identify expected resources, and avoid
breaking production pages unexpectedly.

20
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:57.586
After noise is reduced and required
sources are understood,

21
00:01:57.666 --> 00:02:01.223
the policy can be enforced in stages.

22
00:02:01.303 --> 00:02:05.549
High-value pages may need extra attention.

23
00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:11.941
A good rollout includes monitoring,
ownership, documentation,

24
00:02:12.021 --> 00:02:19.940
and regression checks so future changes do
not quietly weaken or break the policy.
